218
00:15:41,791 --> 00:15:42,012
Rym: Yup.

219
00:15:43,114 --> 00:15:51,890
Rym: But the other thing about Civ games is, and the reason why I'm really on board with your multiplayer first idea is that on one hand I'm old.

220
00:15:52,150 --> 00:15:56,546
Rym: When I was young I could play Civ 2 against AI's single player forever.

221
00:15:56,686 --> 00:15:57,630
Rym: Like all night overnight.

222
00:15:58,010 --> 00:15:58,915
Rym: Because I had infinite time.

223
00:15:58,995 --> 00:15:59,880
Rym: No responsibilities.

224
00:16:00,121 --> 00:16:01,709
Rym: I was young and stupid and it was real fun.

225
00:16:02,310 --> 00:16:03,876
Rym: But as an adult I don't have time for that shit.

226
00:16:03,936 --> 00:16:07,590
Rym: Like I have to ration long single player games that I play.

227
00:16:08,432 --> 00:16:16,850
Rym: But that aside, I have found that Civilization is the most fun when you are playing it with other humans.

228
00:16:18,031 --> 00:16:26,590
Rym: And it is such a different game that I actually have almost zero interest in single player Civ anymore because of how much fucking fun multiplayer is.

229
00:16:26,950 --> 00:16:33,630
Scott: Well single player Civ is basically like, do you know how the AI will behave and can you exploit it?

230
00:16:33,670 --> 00:16:35,677
Scott: Because it's not actually very intelligent.

231
00:16:36,801 --> 00:16:39,630
Scott: So that's what the game comes down to at the higher difficulties.

232
00:16:40,291 --> 00:16:47,690
Rym: Civ 5 is like, or Civ multiplayer, can I do diplomacy with real humans in a real contextual scenario?

233
00:16:48,230 --> 00:16:57,070
Scott: Yeah a lot of the systems in the game, despite it being single player first, only make sense against real humans like trading and making deals and all that.

234
00:16:57,370 --> 00:17:00,369
Scott: And they don't make any sense when you're trying to make a deal with an AI.

235
00:17:03,672 --> 00:17:07,782
Rym: When I knocked you out of that Civ 5 game, I should show you the picture sometime.

236
00:17:07,803 --> 00:17:10,589
